Last Updated: 01 July 2026

CITIS Infotech LLP (“CITIS Infotech”, “CITIS”, “we”, “us” or “our”) respects the privacy of visitors, students, learners, institutions, partners, customers and other users of our website, digital platforms and services.

This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, process and protect personal information when you access our website, register for a programme, submit an enquiry, use our learning platforms or otherwise interact with CITIS Infotech.

1. Information We Collect

Depending on your interaction with us, we may collect:

Personal Information

Name 

Mobile number 

Email address 

Address and location 

Date of birth, where required for programme administration 

Educational qualification 

Institution or organisation details 

Employment or professional information 

Academic and Programme Information

Where applicable, we may collect information relating to:

Course or programme enrolment 

Attendance and participation 

Assessments and examination-related information 

Assignment and project submissions 

Certifications 

Academic progress and learning outcomes 

Technical Information

When you use our website or digital platforms, we may automatically collect certain technical information, including:

IP address 

Browser type 

Device information 

Operating system 

Pages visited 

Date and time of access 

Cookies and similar technologies 

2. How We Use Your Information

CITIS Infotech may use personal information to:

Respond to enquiries and requests 

Provide information about our programmes and services 

Process registrations and enrolments 

Deliver educational and training programmes 

Provide access to learning platforms 

Manage assessments, examinations and certifications 

Communicate programme-related information 

Provide learner support 

Improve our website, products and services 

Conduct analytics and internal reporting 

Manage partnerships and institutional relationships 

Send relevant updates, subject to applicable consent requirements 

Comply with legal, regulatory and contractual obligations 

3. Sharing of Information

We may share relevant information with authorised third parties where necessary for the delivery of our services, including:

Universities and educational institutions 

Schools and colleges 

Technology partners 

Learning Management System providers 

Certification bodies 

Assessment partners 

Internship and placement partners 

Payment service providers 

Government or regulatory authorities, where legally required 

Information will be shared only where reasonably necessary for the relevant service, programme, transaction or legal requirement.

4. Data Security

CITIS Infotech takes reasonable administrative, technical and organisational measures to protect personal information against unauthorised access, misuse, alteration, loss or disclosure.

However, no method of electronic transmission or storage is completely secure. While we take reasonable precautions, we cannot guarantee absolute security of information transmitted through the internet.

5. Cookies

Our website may use cookies and similar technologies to improve user experience, understand website usage and support certain website functions.

Users may manage or disable cookies through their browser settings. However, disabling cookies may affect certain features or functionality of the website.

6. Data Retention

We retain personal information for as long as reasonably necessary to:

Deliver the requested services 

Maintain academic and programme records 

Meet contractual requirements 

Comply with legal and regulatory obligations 

Resolve disputes 

Enforce our agreements 

Retention periods may vary depending on the nature of the information and the applicable programme or service.

7. Children's Information

Certain CITIS programmes are designed for school students and minors. In such cases, personal information may be collected and processed through the relevant school, parent, guardian or authorised institution, as applicable.

Where required, appropriate consent or authorisation from a parent, guardian or educational institution will be obtained or relied upon in accordance with applicable requirements.

8. Third-Party Websites

Our website may contain links to third-party websites, platforms or services. CITIS Infotech is not responsible for the privacy practices, content or security of such third-party websites.

Users are encouraged to review the privacy policies of third-party platforms before providing personal information.

9. Your Rights and Requests

Subject to applicable law, you may contact us regarding your personal information, including requests relating to:

Access to your information 

Correction or updating of information 

Withdrawal of consent, where applicable 

Questions regarding how your information is processed 

10. Changes to This Privacy Policy

CITIS Infotech may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any revised version will be published on this website with an updated effective date.

11. Contact Us

For privacy-related questions or requests, please contact:

